# Scripts
scripts/
*.sh

# ── Re-includes for the `test` build stage ──────────────────────────
# The exclusions above (tests/, *.sh, .env.*) would otherwise make
# `docker build --target test` fail outright on its COPY steps.
# These enter the build CONTEXT only: the production stage never COPYs
# them, so the shipped image is unaffected. Note .env itself stays
# excluded above - real secrets must never enter the context.
!tests/
!unit_tests.sh
!.env.test
